WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.880
Hey you, so nice of you to join&nbsp;
us! We want to tell you about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.920
something that changed kurzgesagt forever.
Kurzgesagt started out as a small-scale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.320
passion project. But creating animated&nbsp;
science videos that are free for everyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.360
doesn’t pay the bills – DAMN YOU reality!&nbsp;
In order to make ends meet we had to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:23.560
on “real jobs” during the day and create&nbsp;
kurzgesagt videos at night. It was tough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.760
but our dream of inspiring people&nbsp;
all around the world kept us going.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.720
Then in 2016 everything changed.
Kurzgesagt’s founder, Philipp Dettmer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.760
had an idea. He wanted to create something&nbsp;
inspiring that would extend beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.200
digital YouTube cosmos. Something tangible.
Something that would represent kurzgesagt’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.400
view of the world and our belief in&nbsp;
humanity’s potential for greatness.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:53.280
His idea: the kurzgesagt Human Era Calendar.&nbsp;
It establishes a new year zero to include all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.120
people and cultures around the world. This&nbsp;
new year zero, roughly 12,000 years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.000
signifies a time when humans first started&nbsp;
working together on a larger scale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.920
laying the foundation for modern society&nbsp;
and eventually our future ahead of us.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.320
The first Human Era Calendar was a&nbsp;
huge success, it sold out within a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.920
few hours and inspired thousands of birbs&nbsp;
around the globe. Every year since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.840
we’ve created a new edition of the Human&nbsp;
Era Calendar – each one more spectacular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.200
and successful than the last. It has&nbsp;
enabled us to grow our team, improve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.360
our video quality and research standards, and&nbsp;
still release our videos for free for everyone.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.280
This year’s calendar is extra special.&nbsp;
Join us as we conduct a series of space&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.280
experiments to see how they would affect the&nbsp;
development of life. What would a creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.520
living near an orange dwarf look like?&nbsp;
Could life still exist after a supernova&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:48.280
explosion? And what the hell is this?
Join us in 12,024 and find out. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.000
of course you can also use it to plan&nbsp;
humanity's next steps towards greatness.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.920
To celebrate what may be our most&nbsp;
glorious calendar yet, we've prepared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.400
a few spectacular limited deals for you.
Thank you so much for being a part of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.449
story and for coming together every&nbsp;
year to make all of this possible!

